@startuml 05-state-driver
!include _style.puml
title Virtual Weather Station - Driver life cycle (vws.ko)

[*] --> UNLOADED

UNLOADED --> LOADED : insmod\ncdev_add, class_register,\ndevice_create, sysfs, procfs
LOADED --> OPEN : first open("/dev/vws")\natomic_inc_return(readers) == 1
OPEN --> STREAMING : hrtimer_start(period)

STREAMING --> STREAMING : timer tick\nconvert -> push -> wake
STREAMING --> STREAMING : read() / poll() / ioctl()
STREAMING --> OPEN : another process opens or closes\n(readers still > 0)

STREAMING --> CLOSED : last close()\natomic_dec_and_test,\nhrtimer_cancel under cfg_lock
CLOSED --> OPEN : reopened
CLOSED --> UNLOADED : rmmod
LOADED --> UNLOADED : rmmod

LOADED : device node and attributes exist,\nsampling clock stopped
STREAMING : hrtimer re-arms itself from\nvd->period on every expiry

note right of CLOSED #FFF8DC
  hrtimer_cancel() is called while cfg_lock
  is still held. Dropping the lock first let a
  concurrent open() start the timer between
  the decrement and the cancel, and have its
  stream killed off immediately.
end note

note bottom
  Configuration through sysfs or ioctl is legal in every state from LOADED on.
  Only sampling needs an open file descriptor, which is what makes the sampling
  clock stop when nobody is listening.
end note
@enduml
